	You can safely enchant weapons or elven armor (or cornuthaums if
you're a wizard) when they're at +5, or other armor when it's at +3. If
you use a blessed scroll, you have a good chance of getting two
additional points, for a total +7 or +5, out of it.

	If you're unlucky and it only gives you one point, for +6/+4,
it's not safe to enchant again. There are various ways to get it back
down to +5/+3 so you can try again, but I seldom find it worth the
bother.


